        "se": "For $y\\ne0$, separate variables: $\\frac{dy}{y}=3\\,dx$, so $\\ln|y|=3x+C$ and $|y|=e^Ce^{3x}$. Absorb the sign into a real constant $A$ to obtain $y=Ae^{3x}$. The zero solution is also included by allowing $A=0$; thus $A\\in\\mathbb R$."
